CSAE — Cascaded Sparse Autoencoders
====================================

This project builds on several open-source works. We gratefully acknowledge:

- dictionary_learning (saprmarks et al., MIT License)
  https://github.com/saprmarks/dictionary_learning
  Provides the generic SAE training harness (`trainSAE`). Installed as a
  dependency (see requirements.txt), not vendored.

- The concept insertion/suppression steering protocol follows Pach et al.,
  "Sparse Autoencoders Learn Monosemantic Features in Vision-Language Models"
  (2025, arXiv:2504.02821); see `steering/`.
- The original "Sparse-Autoencoder" educational repository (IParraMartin, MIT
  License) was the starting point of this codebase.

Model backbones are downloaded from their respective providers and are governed
by their own licenses, not this one:

- Qwen/Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct (Qwen team)
- google/gemma-3-4b-it (Google; Gemma Terms of Use)
- llava-hf/llava-1.5-13b-hf (LLaVA)
- facebook/dinov3-vit7b16-pretrain-lvd1689m (Meta; used for HMS reference embeddings)

The CSAE model (`csae/model.py`), the HMS evaluation (`eval_hms.py`), the
steering code (`steering/`), and the data-generation scripts (`data_gen/`) are
released under the MIT License (see LICENSE).
